WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.490
SPEAKER: Let me tell you a
story about moral hazard.

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:07.020
When I was in graduate school, my
officemate went jogging with his wife.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.500
She twisted her ankle and couldn't
walk, which they knew was bad.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.030
So they went to the doctor.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:16.950
They said, we were jogging, she twisted
her ankle, and now she's in pain.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.840
The doctor said, yes, that's bad.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.730
You need an MRI.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.670
Which they thought was
cool, because MRIs are cool.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:25.860
So they went to schedule
the MRI and then

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:29.670
it turned out it was going to cost
them $500 for their deductible

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.450
and then 20% above that.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.160
So the net cost was going to be like
$700, $800, which all of a sudden

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.770
wasn't so cool because they
didn't have that great insurance.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.390
It was graduate student insurance.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.890
So they went back to the doctor and
they said doctor, do we need the MRI?

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:47.850
The doctor said, no, you don't
need the MRI, wait a few days.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.830
If you're better, you'll be fine.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:53.100
If you're not better after a few
days, then you might need surgery

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.780
and you probably need the MRI.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:01:00.240
So they waited, she got
better, they never got the MRI.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:04.590
Had they had insurance completely, so
they wouldn't have to pay anything,

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:08.520
they would have gotten the MRI and
that would have been a moral hazard.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.580
Care that they would have
consumed when clearly they

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.590
did not value the care
at the price of the care.

